.venv/
.env
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# What a live test run records about one account on one day.
tests/local/

# What the board writes down about the mail account it acts on.  Two kinds of
# file, and the second is why this line is load-bearing rather than tidy.
#
# The log holds message identities, folder names, counts and durations, and is
# forbidden a subject, a sender or any part of a body.
#
# A crash file holds the whole failure: every frame and the values in it.  A
# failure part way through a review means the messages being reviewed -- so
# subjects, senders and bodies, in full.  It is allowed to hold that on this
# condition and no other, which makes this exclusion the thing the content
# rests on.  Anything that would move these files somewhere committable has to
# answer for that first.
logs/

# A traceback saved out of the terminal by hand lands where the person was
# standing, which is here.  Same content, same reason.
crash*.txt

# An editor's swap file holds the content of what is open in it, so a swap of
# one of the above is one of the above.
*.swp

# The scripts that make a workspace on the build host.  Kept here because
# this is where they are edited and this is what the board points at, and
# kept out of git because they are the one place a real host, a real group
# and real repository names have to be written down -- which is exactly what
# this history had removed from it once with filter-repo. The board describes
# their command line and nothing else, so nothing here is needed to build it.
workflow/
